OL,3,GNEWSATop GCSE results in Wales see
OL,4,Aslight increase after major changes to
OL,5,Aqualifications
OL,6,
OL,7,FTop GCSE grades in Wales have risen
OL,8,Fslightly following major changes to
OL,9,Fqualifications in the country.
OL,11,FThe proportion of top A* and A grades
OL,12,FGCSE was up 0.1% point to 19.6%, while
OL,13,F62.3% received grades at C or above.
OL,15,FExam bosses said the results indicated
OL,16,F"stability" as the new qualifications
OL,17,Fare phased in, but the overall pass
OL,18,Frate for Wales was slightly down.
OL,23,APub: 19-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBWales NewsC Reg TVFClean Feed
